# Angles

Paid reframe app. The library is private; community Home shipped, and a card appears there only when it is public. Compose Save defaults to Post; the server stores a card private unless the save says otherwise.

- Backend: Hono + Node on Railway (`backend/`). Not Cloudflare Workers.
- iOS: SwiftUI, iOS 17+, `URLSession` only (`AnglesApp/`). Run on **Joe’s iPhone**, not Simulator.
- LLM: `backend/src/lib/llmClient.ts` only. Never from the app.
- Screen/feature order is `BUILD.md`. Build only the current item. Update that file in the same change as every new screen or feature.
- Do not add SwiftData until that row in `BUILD.md` is next (or the user asked for that task). StoreKit, Drizzle, and Auth have shipped.
- `POST /cards` only stores a cook signed by `/reframe` (`backend/src/lib/cookSignature.ts`); never loosen that to trust client content.
- `POST /reframe` never stores cards or thought text; it may write only text-free metering/idempotency metadata and provider token/cost records.
- Keep `backend/src/types/index.ts` and `ReframeModels.swift` JSON-identical.
- Do not log user thought text. Do not add browser CORS.
- Auth is Better Auth (Sign in with Apple). Owner seam is `requireAuth` / `getOwnerUserId()` in `authStub.ts`. DB is Postgres + Drizzle (`postgres` driver).
- Prefer failing a multi-style reframe over a partial `results` array.
